# Sourced by scripts/smoke-pod. The "Pod" template is a built-in default
# (backend=pod, no command of its own). The smoke has no Claude login, so it
# asks for a login shell in the PTY; the entrypoint still boots, clones and
# seeds the brief before the agent spawns it.
SESSION_SPEC='{"name":"__NAME__","template":"Pod","command":["bash","-l"]}'
# The boot log also names the Claude posture the pod came up with (WI-3243):
# the driven-session policy, the MCP file, and the policy and conversation
# hooks. The marker requires all four, so a pod that lost any of them fails the
# smoke at bootstrap.
BOOT_MARKER='session-entrypoint: claude posture: settings mcp-config policy-hook session-hook$'
